.TH TRYX 1 "2026-09-06" "TRYX Panorama Manager 2.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tryx \- inspect and manage the local TRYX runtime from a terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tryx
.B \-\-help
.br
.B tryx
.B \-\-version
.br
.B tryx
.RI [ \-\-json ]
.B status
.br
.B tryx
.RI [ \-\-json ]
.B capabilities
.br
.B tryx
.RI [ \-\-json ]
.B operations
.br
.B tryx
.RI [ \-\-json ]
.B prepare-downgrade-v10
.br
.B tryx
.RI [ \-\-json ]
.B abort-downgrade-v10
.br
.B tryx
.RI [ \-\-json ]
.B support-report
.B \-\-output-dir
.I ABSOLUTE_DIR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tryx
is a one-shot command-line client for the background TRYX Panorama runtime
shipped in the same native package.
It connects only to an already available D-Bus user session for the same Unix
user and addresses the existing runtime owner.
It does not start the runtime, access USB directly, open a network listener, or
connect to a remote or system bus.
.PP
Inspection and support-report commands are read-only.
The explicit
.B prepare-downgrade-v10
command validates and latches a safe released-v10 compatibility state, then
waits for that exact runtime owner to stop.
It does not install, remove, or downgrade a package.
.PP
The offline
.B abort-downgrade-v10
command removes a preparation marker only when the safe user-session D-Bus is
available, the runtime service name has no owner, and the marker belongs to the
currently installed runtime executable.
.PP
The supported contract is a local terminal for the same Unix user as the D-Bus
session. Remote terminal qualification is deferred to the project backlog.
The command does not provide graphical forwarding or remote-desktop
functionality.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print a redacted runtime, device, recovery, and count summary from the validated
support-snapshot interface.
.TP
.B capabilities
Print the runtime API version and the allowlisted runtime and device
capabilities available for the current exact device context.
.TP
.B operations
Print at most the 32 most recent redacted operation records, in oldest-to-newest
order within that bounded tail.
.TP
.B prepare-downgrade-v10
Ask a runtime advertising
.B runtime.downgrade-v10-preparation.v1
to prepare its durable state for the released v10 runtime.
Only the exact reply states
.B Empty
and
.B FullFrame
are accepted.
Success is reported only after the original D-Bus owner has remained absent for
a bounded stability check; an owner replacement fails closed.
Run this command before the package downgrade.
.TP
.B abort-downgrade-v10
Cancel a previously prepared v10 downgrade while the runtime is offline.
The command does not use the runtime API or start the runtime.
It fails closed when the runtime service has an owner, the marker is missing,
the installed executable differs, or the marker cannot be validated and
removed durably.
.TP
.B support-report \-\-output-dir ABSOLUTE_DIR
Create a new private support report in an existing absolute directory owned by
the current user.
The command generates the filename and never overwrites an existing path.
A host-only report can still be created with status
.B unavailable
when the user-session bus or runtime is unavailable.
An incompatible runtime, a legacy API 8 runtime, or a runtime without the B3
support-snapshot capability produces a host-only report with status
.B unsupported
and exit status 0.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit one compact UTF-8 JSON version 1 object followed by a newline.
This option may appear once, before the command.
Human-readable output is not a parseable interface.
.TP
.B \-\-output-dir ABSOLUTE_DIR
Select the existing destination directory for
.BR support-report .
Relative, unsafe, group-writable, and other-writable destinations are rejected.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage and exit without initializing D-Bus or a graphical platform.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print
.B tryx VERSION
and exit without initializing D-Bus or a graphical platform.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command succeeded, including a successfully written host-only report.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line arguments.
.TP
.B 3
The user-session D-Bus is unavailable.
.TP
.B 4
The TRYX runtime owner is unavailable.
.TP
.B 5
The runtime API is incompatible.
.TP
.B 6
The requested command or capability is unsupported.
.TP
.B 7
The shared D-Bus deadline expired.
.TP
.B 8
The runtime owner changed during the command.
.TP
.B 9
A runtime D-Bus call failed.
.TP
.B 10
The runtime reply was invalid or did not match the current context.
.TP
.B 11
The report destination is unsafe.
.TP
.B 12
No-clobber publication found an existing destination.
.TP
.B 13
The report could not be written or published safely.
.TP
.B 14
The runtime refused downgrade preparation, or offline downgrade cancellation
could not prove that removing the marker was safe.
.TP
.B 70
An internal software invariant failed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/tryx
Public command-line client.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/tryx-panorama-manager/tryx-panorama-runtime
Private background runtime queried by the client.
.TP
.I ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/tryx-panorama-manager-downgrade-v10/runtime-downgrade-v10.json
Owner-only durable preparation marker for the explicit released-v10 downgrade
workflow. Do not edit or remove it manually; use
.BR "tryx abort-downgrade-v10" .
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/tryx-panorama.service
Systemd user unit that an operator may start separately when required.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
tryx status
tryx --json capabilities
tryx operations
tryx prepare-downgrade-v10
tryx abort-downgrade-v10
tryx support-report --output-dir /home/user/support
.fi
.SH BUGS
Report issues at
.UR https://github.com/DXVSI/Tryx-Linux-GUI/issues
.UE .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tryx-panorama-manager (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.user (5)
